From 09782453e5cf78555ab73413ad324add649f8bbf Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tim Carney <tim.carney@cargt.com>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 11:36:26 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] oei: ddr: cargt: select between several DDR timing
 configurations at runtime

One OEI image boots SOM variants populated with different DRAM parts.

- oei/ddr/cargt_ddr.c (CARGT_MULTI_DDR): use the configuration named by
  the board (Cargt_Ddr_Get_Cfg_Id(); weak, CARGT_DDR_FORCE_ID for tests).
  If it is unknown or fails to train, try the others in list order
  (bootstrap). QuickBoot is only allowed for the identified configuration,
  since saved training data does not record which configuration produced
  it; a QuickBoot failure falls back to a full training.
- Ddrc_Get_Sdram_Type() uses the configuration being initialized
  (g_dram_timing) instead of the single global dram_timing.
- ddr_phy_pie may be shared between configurations, with a per
  configuration {index, value} patch applied while it is loaded.

Without CARGT_MULTI_DDR the behaviour is unchanged.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [Cargt board specific]
